cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "TensorPyPy: Tensor-Aware Meta-Tracing JIT Compiler"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Izawa
    given-names: Yusuke
    affiliation: Tokyo Metropolitan University
license: MIT
abstract: |-
  TensorPyPy is a fork of PyPy whose RPython meta-tracing JIT compiler
  provides a tensor runtime, MetaTensor. Traced chains of tensor operations
  in the Python program become fused GPU kernels. The code is in
  rpython/metatensor/, pypy/module/_metatensor/ and lib_pypy/tensorpypy/,
  and benchmark/ holds the MetaTensor benchmarks.

  benchmark/motion/ contains a prototype of MOTION, a method that derives
  the program transition for a change in the execution environment from
  interpreter code instead of writing it by hand. The example change is
  leave: a worker leaves a group computation before its contribution is
  committed, and a declared reason decides whether that contribution is kept
  or removed.

  The prototype consists of:
  - a 7-line change rule (pypy/module/_metatensor/rule_leave.py), compiled
    by the meta-tracer like other interpreter code;
  - a static check (benchmark/eval/audit_rules.py) that the rule uses only
    the abstract interface in motion_iface.py, and a non-conforming rule
    (benchmark/motion/rule_leave_leaky.py) that the check rejects;
  - an independent checker (benchmark/motion/check_leave.py) that compares
    the generated transition with an interpreter-only run;
  - a hand-written adapter for comparison
    (benchmark/motion/adapter_leave.py), and a script
    (benchmark/motion/count_lines.py) that counts the hand-written lines of
    each.
keywords:
  - PyPy
  - RPython
  - meta-tracing JIT
  - tensor compiler
  - kernel fusion
  - GPU
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "MetaTensor: Tensor Fusion in a Meta-Tracing Compiler"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23298877
    authors:
      - family-names: Izawa
        given-names: Yusuke
